; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Animals from Arcs
; CATEGORY: Classic Logo
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     arcs, ARCR, ARCL, drawing, procedures
; SUMMARY:  A rabbit and a snail drawn only from circles, petals and spirals built on two little helpers, ARCR and ARCL.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Draws a sitting rabbit with long ears and a fluffy tail, and a snail
;   with a spiral shell, on a sunny meadow. Every curve comes from
;   ARCR (an arc turning right) or ARCL (an arc turning left).
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Then try  clean arcr 100 90  and  arcl 50 180  in the
;   command center to see what the helpers do on their own.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * ARCR and ARCL: a circle is "a little forward, a little turn"
;   * a petal or leaf is two arcs with a turn between them
;   * drawing in layers: things at the back are drawn first, and each
;     new FILLED shape covers what is already there
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Give the rabbit a carrot (an orange triangle and a green petal).
;   * Make a second, smaller snail racing the first one.
;   * Draw a duck: a big circle body, a small circle head, a petal beak.
; ============================================================

; Many early Logo manuals handed children two helper procedures much
; like these, often called ARCR and ARCL, so they could draw round
; things before they knew any trigonometry. The turtle really walks the
; arc instead of standing still like the ARC primitive, which is handy
; when you want to know where the turtle ends up.

; Walk DEGREES of a circle of radius R, turning right (or left).
; Each 5-degree step is 2 * pi * R / 72 long.
to arcr :r :degrees
  repeat :degrees / 5 [forward :r * 0.0872665 right 5]
end

to arcl :r :degrees
  repeat :degrees / 5 [forward :r * 0.0872665 left 5]
end

; A filled circle centred on (X, Y): start at its left edge facing up.
to disk :x :y :r :color
  penup setxy :x - :r :y setheading 0 pendown
  filled :color [arcr :r 360]
end

; A petal from (X, Y) pointing in direction DIR. The petal leans 30
; degrees to the right of its first heading, so we start 30 to the left.
to petal :x :y :dir :len :color
  penup setxy :x :y setheading :dir - 30 pendown
  filled :color [arcr :len 60 right 120 arcr :len 60]
end

to rabbit :x :y
  ; from the back to the front: each part covers the ones before it
  setpencolor [120 110 110]
  disk :x - 82 :y - 30 20 [255 255 255]              ; tail
  petal :x - 22 :y + 140 -15 95 [235 230 225]        ; ears
  petal :x + 22 :y + 140 15 95 [235 230 225]
  petal :x - 25 :y + 150 -15 68 [250 190 200]        ; inside of the ears
  petal :x + 25 :y + 150 15 68 [250 190 200]
  disk :x :y 80 [225 220 215]                        ; body
  disk :x :y + 115 45 [235 230 225]                  ; head
  disk :x - 45 :y - 72 22 [235 230 225]              ; front feet
  disk :x + 45 :y - 72 22 [235 230 225]
  ; eyes and nose are DOTs, drawn last so they sit on the face
  setpensize 9 setpencolor 0
  dot list :x - 17 :y + 125
  dot list :x + 17 :y + 125
  setpencolor [230 120 140]
  dot list :x :y + 105
  setpensize 2
end

; The shell is a spiral: a half circle, then a slightly smaller half
; circle, again and again. Drawn after the shell's fill so it shows.
to shell.spiral :r
  if :r < 6 [stop]
  arcl :r 180
  shell.spiral :r * 0.75
end

to snail :x :y
  ; the body first: a long rounded slug shape that the shell sits on
  setpencolor [120 140 60]
  penup setxy :x - 120 :y - 110 setheading 90 pendown
  filled [180 200 100] [forward 230 arcl 25 180 forward 230 arcl 25 180]
  setpencolor [110 70 30]
  disk :x :y 80 [220 150 70]
  penup setxy :x + 80 :y setheading 0 pendown
  setpensize 4
  shell.spiral 80
  setpensize 2
  ; eye stalks with dots on the tips
  setpensize 4
  foreach [-145 -125] [
    penup setxy :x - 112 :y - 64 pendown
    setxy :x + ? :y + 20
    setpensize 12 dot pos setpensize 4
  ]
  setpensize 2
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [200 230 255]
setpensize 2
; the background first: sun in the corner and the meadow
setpencolor [250 200 40]
disk 330 230 45 [255 220 60]
setpencolor [80 160 70]
penup setxy -400 -200 setheading 90 pendown
filled [120 200 100] [forward 800 right 90 forward 100 right 90 forward 800 right 90 forward 100]
rabbit -190 -120
snail 170 -110
